<title>GERMANY: Merged RWE units aim for 120 mln DM div.</title>
<headline>Merged RWE units aim for 120 mln DM div.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>German utility Rheinelektra, banking on efficiencies from its merger with Lahmeyer AG, said on Monday it aimed to raise profit enough to pay a 1996/97 dividend of 120 million marks ($71.6 million).</p>
<p>The dividend would include a bonus aimed at improving tax treatment of dividends for shareholders, the company said.</p>
<p>Both Rheinelektra and Lahmeyer are 60-percent-owned by diversified utility group RWE AG. The merger, announced last month, was expected to be approved at an extraordinary shareholders meeting on February 25.</p>
<p>The combined company will be known as Lahmeyer AG and based in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150 ($ = 1.676 German Marks)</p>
